# Generated by runs.
#
# runs/ is KEPT LOCALLY ONLY — 384MB across 300 files, almost all of it raw
# command stdout. One attempt captured a 221MB GeoJSON dump when the agent
# ran `roads --in "Rhode Island" -f geojsonseq` instead of counting.
#
# It cannot go to this remote as-is: GitHub hard-rejects files over 100MB.
# The options were to cap the stdout, drop the oversized files, or add
# git-lfs; we chose none of them. The evidence we actually reason from —
# baselines, logs, artifacts, the question bank and proposals — is versioned
# beside this file. The raw payloads are not, and live only on the machine
# that produced them.
#
# If these ever need to leave this machine, cap stdout at 4KB and keep the
# original byte counts: that is 9.2MB with no files dropped.
experiments/runs/

# Everything else under experiments/ IS versioned — baselines, logs and the
# supporting research are the evidence our conclusions rest on.

# Agent scratch space
.pi-subagents/

# The previous TypeScript implementation — kept on disk for reference, but not
# part of what this project ships.
_ts_archive/

